{
    "allowed_use": "Whether the L2-served fraction of a grouped operand stream depends on the resident working set, at a fixed sharing structure. The discriminating quantity is the presence and position of a knee, not the absolute rate.",
    "consequence": "A DRAM-served fraction indexed by occupancy or reuse footprint cannot express a shortfall that is flat in footprint. The residency-profile shape carried by the shared miss core is the wrong abstraction for this phenomenon and must not be filled with it.",
    "dram_read_capability_bytes_per_s": {
        "metax_c500": 1653069600000.0,
        "nvidia_a800": 1790532000000.0
    },
    "finding": "The probe detects a capacity knee where one must exist: nvidia_a800 holds a flat 45-50 percent served fraction from a 0.06 MiB working set through 16.5 MiB and then falls to 34.3 and 24.1 percent at 33.0 and 66.0 MiB, bracketing its 40 MiB L2. metax_c500 shows no such knee at its documented 8 MiB. Its served fraction is flat near 33 percent from 0.13 MiB through 8.25 MiB and is still 30.2 percent at 16.5 MiB, declining only in the same far region as nvidia_a800, where a single program's own K stream no longer fits any cache. The metax_c500 shortfall is therefore not a residency effect: it does not depend on the working set at all across a 128x range that spans its capacity. It is a level difference. Against the 68.3 percent a same-K-step sharing model predicts for this structure, nvidia_a800 realizes about 46 percent and metax_c500 about 33 percent. The 49 percent level that 'the repeatedly referenced object shares and the streamed object does not' would produce sits just above nvidia_a800's plateau and well above metax_c500's.",
    "forbidden_use": "An absolute DRAM bandwidth, an L2 capacity, a production operator duration, a per-shape traffic correction, or any parameter chosen to move a production MAPE.",
