        "method": "Object size fixed at 8 KiB; the N tile count moves the sharing shape while the program count and logical request volume stay fixed. A 104/108 program wave then spans ceil(W/n) A streams and min(W,n) B streams.",
        "metric_confound": "The apparent served fraction is 1 - configured_dram_read_capability / logical_byte_rate, which credits every byte the probe does not achieve to L2 service and therefore assumes DRAM runs at its capability. The monotone dependence on stream count is the signature of achieved DRAM bandwidth scaling with memory-level parallelism, not of L2 service, so for metax_c500 this metric cannot separate 'L2 served less' from 'DRAM delivered less than its capability'. Separating them needs a DRAM byte counter, which on this target is mcProfiler and is a host-global serial resource. The knee result above is unaffected: its stream count is fixed at 66 throughout, so the confound is constant across it and the absence of a knee at 8 MiB stands.",
